codex
A stronger variance-reduction idea is to stop MC one layer early: estimate the penultimate mean/covariance from samples, then compute the final ReLU mean with a Gaussian preactivation approximation. The last preactivation is a width-256 sum, so this CLT-style correction may be accurate enough to beat raw final MC.
